# Drive the server without a client. Needs the REST Client extension
# (humao.rest-client) — already listed in .vscode/extensions.json.
#
# Start the server first: Run Task -> "serve", or F5 -> "mapd (server)".
#
# Click "Send Request" above any block. Run "new game" first: the other
# requests read its game_id out of the response.
#
# Because `rows` is plain text, you can read the dungeon directly in the
# response pane.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@game = {{new.response.body.game_id}}

### health
GET {{host}}/healthz

# @name new
### new game — seed is optional, and is the ONLY thing a client may choose
POST {{host}}/v1/games
Content-Type: application/json

{"seed": 1234}

### the current frame, without touching the game
GET {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/frame

### move
POST {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/command
Content-Type: application/json

{"key": "Down"}

### wait a turn in place
POST {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/command
Content-Type: application/json

{"key": "."}

### pick up whatever is here — may answer with a prompt instead of a frame
POST {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/command
Content-Type: application/json

{"key": ","}

### drop something — always opens a picker when anything is carried
POST {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/command
Content-Type: application/json

{"key": "D"}

### answer an open prompt with a letter (or a direction, for a throw)
POST {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/command
Content-Type: application/json

{"key": "A"}

### cancel an open prompt — any non-matching key does, and costs no turn
POST {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/command
Content-Type: application/json

{"key": "Escape"}

### descend
POST {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/command
Content-Type: application/json

{"key": ">"}

### read-only views: inventory | look | status | help — none costs a turn
GET {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/views/inventory

###
GET {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/views/look

###
GET {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/views/status

###
GET {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/views/help

### replay a whole script in one round trip — this is what a bug report is
POST {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/commands
Content-Type: application/json

{"keys": ["Down", "Down", "Right", ",", "."]}

### an unbound key is NOT an error: it wastes a turn, as it always has
POST {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/command
Content-Type: application/json

{"key": "banana"}

### dungeon settings are server policy — this must be refused with 400
POST {{host}}/v1/games
Content-Type: application/json

{"seed": 1, "hidden_door_percent": 0, "num_rooms": 40}

### unknown view — 404, and the error lists the real ones
GET {{host}}/v1/games/{{game}}/views/spellbook

### unknown game — 404
GET {{host}}/v1/games/nope/frame
